    risks: "Pneumothorax and airway bleeding are the principal procedure-specific risks; either may require a chest tube, bronchoscopy, transfusion or admission. Other risks include hypoxaemia, bronchospasm, infection, sedative reaction, arrhythmia and non-diagnostic or misleadingly small samples. Severe haemorrhage or respiratory failure is uncommon but possible.",
