    evaluation: "Assessment uses vital signs, oxygen and chest imaging; ultrasound is expected for fluid-site selection when feasible. Fluid indication, loculation, coagulation, anticoagulants and analgesia are reviewed. The plan names catheter size, sampling, underwater seal, suction criteria, flushing, imaging, removal and escalation for persistent leak or infection.",
    technique: "With sterile preparation, monitoring, analgesia and local anaesthetic, the operator enters above the rib to reduce neurovascular injury. Seldinger placement dilates over a guidewire; blunt dissection creates a tract for a larger tube. The drain is secured, connected to a one-way seal, labelled and imaged for position where indicated; clamping is not routine in a bubbling pneumothorax.",
